  "period_note": "CONSOLIDATED (Group) basis, matching this bank's main Q4/annual series (see sources.json reporting_basis). Source: Southeast Bank's own BSEC-mandated 'Evaluation of the Quarterly Financials by the Audit Committee and by the Board' disclosure table, embedded in its annual report (a corporate-governance disclosure most banks answer with a checkbox, but which Southeast Bank answers with an actual Q1/Q2/Q3/Q4 balance-sheet-and-income-statement table for that report's own year, plus a comparative column for the prior year). Balance-sheet line items are the 1 January to 31 March 2025 period-end snapshot (basis reported). Income-statement line items and EPS are CUMULATIVE FROM 1 JANUARY 2025 (\"1 January to 31 March 2025\" exactly as the table's own column header states), not discrete-quarter figures -- flagged via the _cumulative suffix, basis reported, same convention as CITYBANK. Balance-sheet identity (Total assets = Total liabilities + Total equity + Non-controlling interest) holds to within BDT 1m rounding. Cumulative net profit after tax increases monotonically Q1->Q2->Q3 within 2025 (validated; no violation). Most recent year in the archive; no later report exists yet to provide an independent cross-check (same situation as the FY2025 annual entry). NOTABLE: for the first time since FY2018, Q4 is NOT a discrete loss quarter -- cumulative net profit rose from 1,957m (9-month) to 3,350m (full year), a strong discrete Q4-alone profit of roughly 1,393m, even though the cumulative loan-loss provision still rose substantially in Q4 (5,272m at 9-month to 7,484m at year-end, a ~2,212m discrete charge) -- consistent with the bank being past the FY2024 credit-quality trough (see the existing 2024_Q4.json period_note).",
